  {
   "id": "snoop-dotson-texans-final",
   "kind": "chapter",
   "club": "Eagles",
   "headline": "The One That Got Away, and the Linebacker Who Came Back Better",
   "body": [
    "Y90 is the season Philadelphia still turns over. The Eagles went 14-3 and reached Super Bowl CXLIX, and the Texans won it 32-22. Dotson was not whole for all of it: injury cost him 2 games, 18 played to the 20 Akiem Brock logged. He still made 75 tackles, his overall rating jumped from 66 to 71, and his grade rose to S, where it has stayed in every season since.",
    "The answer came in Y91. Healthy for all 20 games, he made 95 tackles with 3 sacks and 2 forced fumbles, the Eagles went 15-2 and beat the Raiders 38-23 in Super Bowl CL, and his overall climbed to 79. Y92 brought 4 sacks, another title, 30-21 over the Colts, and a rating of 84. The depth player from Y89 had become a linebacker opponents game-planned around."
   ],
