  {
   "id": "snoop-dotson-dynasty",
   "kind": "chapter",
   "club": "Eagles",
   "headline": "Five Straight Februaries, and the Steadiest Defender of the Eagles Dynasty",
   "body": [
    "From Y93 to Y97 the Eagles won every Super Bowl, and Dotson won every one with them, his ring count climbing from 3 to 8. Philadelphia went 17-0 in Y93 and again in Y95, and the linebacker played all 20 games of both seasons.",
    "His best tackling year was Y95: 102 of them, with 3 sacks. Y96 was the most complete. He had 4 sacks, 5 interceptions and 2 forced fumbles across 21 games, and his Career Legacy passed 7,500, the Hall of Fame bar, for the first time. His overall reached 96 that season and 98 the next.",
    "Y97 was the one dent. Injury cost him a game, 19 played to the 20 Brock logged, and he managed only 1 sack. He made 90 tackles anyway, and Philadelphia beat the Colts 38-22. Nobody knew it yet, but it was his last game in green."
   ],
