  {
   "id": "snoop-dotson-chicago",
   "kind": "chapter",
   "club": "Bears",
   "headline": "Skura Goes to Chicago, and His Linebacker Goes With Him",
   "body": [
    "After Y97, Dorren Skura left Philadelphia for the Bears, and in his first season there the coach brought Dotson to Chicago. Much of the dynasty stayed behind: Bones Crawford and Akiem Brock are still Eagles. At 32, Dotson started over in a new city beside a young quarterback, JJ Starling, who threw for 5,019 yards that season.",
    "Chicago went 16-1. Dotson played all 20 games, made 85 tackles and added 3 sacks, which lifted his career total to 26, past the 24 that Deshone Bello and Kalif Suh share. Only the 112 T. Watt holds on Skura's own record board, from the Dolphins in Y6, stands above him.",
    "The playoffs ran through old enemies. The Giants fell 46-25 in the divisional round, making the coach's record against them 20-0 across the Eagles and Bears years. Washington went down 40-29, and in Super Bowl CLVII Chicago held off the Dolphins 40-38. Dotson had his ninth ring, the first he ever won away from Philadelphia."
   ],
